<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49855" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūnĭversālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.
		universus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to all</i> or
				<i>the whole</i>, <i>universal</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecepta universalia vel perpetualia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 13, 14</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaestiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					5, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 5, 12</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					5, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nihil inveniebam aut proprium aut universale,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 10, 71, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
